{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>Your statutes</b> — A man in his dwelling place is astonished, and the opposite is זמירות [songs]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "The lemma reads זמרות (from the verse), while the body contrasts it with the reverse wordplay on זמירות; the pun on מגורי/משתומם is preserved hyper-literally as the passage appears deliberately cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:27.187098995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}